WEBVTT


00:00:47.030 --> 00:00:50.356
LEFT BEHIND


00:01:22.331 --> 00:01:23.144
Hello.


00:01:23.196 --> 00:01:24.187
Hi Mom!


00:01:24.573 --> 00:01:27.565
Chloe, welcome home.
You're home, right?


00:01:27.565 --> 00:01:29.432
Yup, safe and sound.


00:01:29.473 --> 00:01:31.394
Your brother has been bouncing off the walls.


00:01:31.394 --> 00:01:33.842
Oh, I can't wait to see him.


00:01:34.958 --> 00:01:37.367
So, is everything up for
dad's surprise party?


00:01:37.597 --> 00:01:41.789
Um, Honey, I'm afraid your dad's not
gonna be here when you get home.


00:01:42.008 --> 00:01:42.779
What?


00:01:44.010 --> 00:01:46.253
Why not? Mom, what happened?


00:01:46.879 --> 00:01:48.224
He got called in to work.


00:01:48.474 --> 00:01:52.645
Did you tell him I was coming?
- Yeah, Honey, I did but...


00:01:53.230 --> 00:01:54.533
They called this morning
and, eh...


00:01:54.533 --> 00:01:55.629
What is his flight?


00:01:57.339 --> 00:02:00.332
It's London.
-3:35?


00:02:02.918 --> 00:02:05.012
Honey, don't make it hard...
-Tell Raymie I'll be home before supper.


00:02:22.085 --> 00:02:24.057
You must feel like
you've seen it all.


00:02:24.192 --> 00:02:28.040
You seemed to be in the middle of a new disaster
every time I turned on the news.


00:02:28.061 --> 00:02:32.128
Oh, what is the old adage?
'It's a dirty job but someone's gotta do it'.


00:02:32.139 --> 00:02:34.871
Can I ask you a question,
Mr. Williams?


00:02:34.955 --> 00:02:35.943
Yeah, sure.


00:02:35.985 --> 00:02:37.956
Do you read the Bible?
-Well...


00:02:39.124 --> 00:02:41.961
I guess not as often
as you do.


00:02:42.055 --> 00:02:48.949
Well, Matthew 24:7 says there shall be famines,
pestilences and earthquakes in diverse places.


00:02:48.949 --> 00:02:53.015
All of these things, the disasters, the wars,
they are all signs.


00:02:53.192 --> 00:02:56.186
So, God knew all these things
were going to happen?


00:02:56.228 --> 00:02:58.095
Honey, God knows everything.


00:02:58.126 --> 00:03:00.931
So, why didn't He do something?


00:03:01.098 --> 00:03:05.948
I mean, He is God, right?
Couldn't He stop the flood if He wanted to?
Maybe, sent a little rain for the famine...


00:03:05.989 --> 00:03:11.078
It's a fallen world. God created it perfect
and we destroyed it on the first set...


00:03:11.088 --> 00:03:13.121
Who destroyed it? Me?...


00:03:14.028 --> 00:03:15.154
You? Him?


00:03:15.196 --> 00:03:18.168
The Lord works...
-... in mysterious ways, I know.


00:03:19.107 --> 00:03:24.217
But somehow, people keep believing
He loves them. Now, that is mysterious.


00:03:30.256 --> 00:03:32.164
Sorry to interrupt.


00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:28.238
Going my way?


00:04:55.268 --> 00:04:57.301
I enjoyed your speech.


00:04:59.210 --> 00:05:01.274
Yeah, sorry about that ...
- Now, don't be.


00:05:01.316 --> 00:05:03.288
That was really good.


00:05:04.091 --> 00:05:06.113
I'm assuming it's not your first time
making it.


00:05:06.228 --> 00:05:09.190
Well, the first time aloud.
-Cameron Williams.


00:05:10.233 --> 00:05:12.223
'Buck'... my friends.


00:05:17.313 --> 00:05:19.346
I'm...eh, Chloe Steele.


00:05:19.357 --> 00:05:21.286
'Chloe' to my friends.


00:05:23.226 --> 00:05:25.092
So, you're in college.


00:05:25.134 --> 00:05:29.160
Wow, that investigative journalism.
it really pays off.


00:05:29.202 --> 00:05:33.154
I just wanted to say thank you
for rescuing me from that nutty lady.


00:05:33.154 --> 00:05:34.385
Oh, thank my mom.


00:05:34.385 --> 00:05:36.376
She, as you would,
have been rehearsing for it.


00:05:36.397 --> 00:05:39.256
Oh, is she... pretty?


00:05:39.256 --> 00:05:41.258
Nutty...


00:05:43.373 --> 00:05:50.109
Actually, I was looking through the thesaurus I've found
this morning, I've decided to go with 'Wacko'.


00:05:50.318 --> 00:05:52.217
Wacko?


00:05:52.217 --> 00:05:54.209
I like that word, 'Wacko'.


00:05:56.295 --> 00:05:58.328
Can I buy you a coffee?


00:05:59.235 --> 00:06:01.394
No, no, I'm fine.


00:06:01.405 --> 00:06:03.198
Come on!


00:06:03.344 --> 00:06:08.288
What if I throw in one of those fantastic
little boxes with the strawberry jam...


00:06:08.319 --> 00:06:12.261
Oh, my God...
Wow, well, that is... that's tempting.


00:06:12.261 --> 00:06:13.385
Yes? .
- Hmm hmm.


00:06:13.396 --> 00:06:18.371
But I'm waiting for someone, and he
should be here any minute.


00:06:22.375 --> 00:06:24.441
My Dad.


00:06:25.421 --> 00:06:29.155
I flew home to surprise him
for his birthday, but...


00:06:29.155 --> 00:06:31.157
...something came up.


00:06:42.358 --> 00:06:44.348
Well, have a safe flight...


00:06:48.196 --> 00:06:50.302
Hi, sweet heart!
-Hi!


00:06:52.315 --> 00:06:56.217
What are you doing here?
-Well, I came home to surprise you
on your birthday.


00:06:56.289 --> 00:06:59.313
Honey, I just got called in.
There's no way I can get out of it now.


00:06:59.355 --> 00:07:02.379
Yeah, that's what mom said...
-I wished that you would've told me
you would be coming.


00:07:03.235 --> 00:07:07.396
Oh wait... you, you're Cameron Williams,
Holy cow...


00:07:07.438 --> 00:07:10.337
So you two?
-Oh, we just met.


00:07:10.451 --> 00:07:12.381
Hi, it's a pleasure, Captain.
- Ray.


00:07:13.226 --> 00:07:19.263
Well, I'm gonna let you two catch up, yeah.
And eh... it was really nice to meet you, Chloe.


00:07:19.305 --> 00:07:21.421
You look great.
- Thank you.


00:07:21.432 --> 00:07:23.371
Let's talk somewhere.


00:07:24.372 --> 00:07:26.468
How was school?
- It's Good.


00:07:26.521 --> 00:07:28.481
Good, yeah...


00:07:33.320 --> 00:07:34.489
What?


00:07:35.469 --> 00:07:39.369
You know the first thing I thought
when mom told me you're not gonna be home?


00:07:39.442 --> 00:07:40.505
It's that you left.


00:07:41.308 --> 00:07:48.482
I mean, really left. Just packed up your bags,
slammed the doors, squealed the tyres
and just drove off.


00:07:49.316 --> 00:07:51.455
Your mom and I are fine, Chloe.


00:07:51.538 --> 00:07:55.366
It's okay, I don't blame you.


00:07:55.407 --> 00:07:58.432
You don't blame me for what?
- For running away.


00:07:58.443 --> 00:08:01.446
But I didn't run away.
You said, you thought I run away.


00:08:02.488 --> 00:08:05.482
Who is that girl?
- What girl?


00:08:06.431 --> 00:08:10.394
That flight attendant,
beautiful, blonde one.


00:08:11.374 --> 00:08:15.400
Flight attendant...
I worked with dozens of flight attendants.
.


00:08:15.452 --> 00:08:17.441
Don't even know her name.


00:08:19.350 --> 00:08:26.463
If this was a year ago, you know before
mom drank with collate, you'd be home by now.


00:08:27.297 --> 00:08:30.478
We would be all be home,
like a family or something.


00:08:31.312 --> 00:08:36.340
Chloe, I... I think you know that your mom and
I got married when we were both very young...


00:08:36.392 --> 00:08:41.334
...and the changes that a person goes through
between 20 and 50 are enormous.


00:08:41.501 --> 00:08:47.467
She's just doing what she believes is right
and maybe you should cut her some slack.


00:08:47.509 --> 00:08:52.461
Me?... How about you?
You're the one on the way to London.


00:08:52.492 --> 00:08:55.360
You are a one who has not been home
since Christmas.


00:08:55.360 --> 00:08:57.519
I  have school .
- And I have a job.


00:08:58.530 --> 00:09:02.567
I just feel like she's always trying
to shove it down my throat.


00:09:04.350 --> 00:09:09.418
I know... Look, I know that this past year,
has been something of an adjustment, but...


00:09:09.554 --> 00:09:14.403
She is your mother, and I think it'd be good
if you, no, if we both...


00:09:14.403 --> 00:09:16.594
...could be a little more supportive.


00:09:18.450 --> 00:09:21.534
You missed her...
- Yes, I do.


00:09:22.348 --> 00:09:26.385
But hey, if she's gonna run off with another man,
why not Jesus, huh?


00:09:28.626 --> 00:09:30.462
Where is your ring?


00:09:35.541 --> 00:09:39.578
It's in my car.
I never wear it when I fly.


00:09:42.393 --> 00:09:47.431
Chloe, your mom means the world to me,
I'm not going to do anything to mess it up.
Okay?


00:09:48.411 --> 00:09:51.433
And I have to go.
We'll talk when I get back.


00:09:51.610 --> 00:09:53.581
Not gonna be here
when you get back.


00:09:53.581 --> 00:09:57.419
Oh, but you'll gonna be back home
again soon, right?


00:09:59.432 --> 00:10:00.486
Here...


00:10:00.600 --> 00:10:05.460
The car is in the usual spot,
and go easy on mom.
She'll come around.


00:10:06.440 --> 00:10:08.442
I love you.


00:10:38.435 --> 00:10:39.603
Are you okay?


00:10:41.481 --> 00:10:44.546
Yes, yes, I'm fine.


00:10:50.533 --> 00:10:53.524
Investigative journalist, remember?


00:10:54.671 --> 00:10:57.581
Right.
- Yeah.


00:11:06.665 --> 00:11:08.656
So...


00:11:08.698 --> 00:11:11.733
I'm just a little disappointed,
that's all.


00:11:12.578 --> 00:11:16.614
It was a big deal to me.
All of us together, having a good time.


00:11:16.655 --> 00:11:19.555
Well, I'm sure you would have stayed
if he could.


00:11:24.099 --> 00:11:26.737
The turkey... a vulture


00:11:26.738 --> 00:11:30.639
...comes up to the gate and dropped two dead rabbits onto the floor.


00:11:30.712 --> 00:11:33.684
And the flight attendant says...
"I'm sorry...


00:11:33.715 --> 00:11:36.594
...we only allowed one carrier."


00:11:36.656 --> 00:11:39.566
I'm sorry Captain, that's bad.


00:11:39.639 --> 00:11:42.497
That is always funny.


00:11:42.539 --> 00:11:45.698
Well, if you have anymore bad jokes,
you can always come and find me.


00:11:54.801 --> 00:11:57.731
Hey Marcus, they got that computer problems figured out?


00:11:57.731 --> 00:12:02.507
Negative that, Pentagon,
apparently, some of the equipment on the flight deck are outdated.


00:12:03.551 --> 00:12:07.681
Yeah, you had me flying east, in
6 hours time, I would be 9 hours older.


00:12:07.900 --> 00:12:12.623
Do that for about 6 years and maybe
you'll catch up to me. Happy Birthday Buddy,
Have a good flight.


00:12:12.624 --> 00:12:13.761
Thanks.


00:12:17.672 --> 00:12:19.778
Sounds like that's all
your mom talks about.


00:12:20.644 --> 00:12:22.782
Seems like it sometimes.


00:12:25.596 --> 00:12:31.802
Hate someone who sees earthquake
on the news and then tries to
convince everyone it's a good thing.


00:12:32.636 --> 00:12:34.669
Does that make sense to you?


00:12:35.847 --> 00:12:40.812
The day after Tsunami,
there's that one woman, Medina.


00:12:41.563 --> 00:12:45.839
She lost three of her four children in that wave,
dragged down to the sea while she watched.


00:12:46.600 --> 00:12:50.771
It was all she could do was to hold on to a tree
with a six-week old baby in her arms.


00:12:52.649 --> 00:12:58.789
And she was so sure that God
had saved her and the baby
that she went straight to her knees.


00:12:59.655 --> 00:13:03.576
She thanked Him.


00:13:03.670 --> 00:13:05.830
She thanked Him for
killing the others?


00:13:07.613 --> 00:13:16.686
She's got the chance, that night she refused
to leave the evacuation and
after all God was watching over her.


00:13:17.770 --> 00:13:19.794
And....
- Mudslide...


00:13:21.775 --> 00:13:24.717
Buried the whole village
under 10-feet of slime.


00:13:24.717 --> 00:13:27.843
How do people see some things 'like that',
and just...


00:13:28.719 --> 00:13:32.756
If you look hard enough, you'll see
whatever it is you're looking for.


00:13:33.798 --> 00:13:37.636
But you might have to ignore
a lot of other things to do it.


00:13:38.783 --> 00:13:41.682
One of them...


00:13:41.849 --> 00:13:43.873
...might be the truth.


00:13:44.853 --> 00:13:46.845
And what about you?


00:13:47.732 --> 00:13:49.817
What did you see in that village?


00:13:52.705 --> 00:13:57.775
I saw a lot of people who'd lost everything
that ever mattered.


00:13:58.722 --> 00:14:01.693
Did you ask why?


00:14:01.725 --> 00:14:03.811
I know why.


00:14:03.853 --> 00:14:05.886
Tsunami.


00:14:05.896 --> 00:14:07.774
You know what I mean.


00:14:08.796 --> 00:14:10.862
No, No, I didn't.


00:14:11.915 --> 00:14:15.877
If you had to find a reason for something
like that to happen, then...


00:14:17.890 --> 00:14:20.884
Well, You might end up behind
a stranger at the airport?


00:14:23.835 --> 00:14:25.702
Oh...


00:14:25.869 --> 00:14:28.903
Love that laugh.
- Oh, no.


00:14:33.762 --> 00:14:34.919
What?


00:14:34.930 --> 00:14:38.882
Oh, just thinking about Ray's joke.
That guy cracks me up.


00:14:38.934 --> 00:14:42.803
Ray? You mean Captain Steele?


00:14:43.679 --> 00:14:45.744
Only infront of other people.


00:14:46.756 --> 00:14:47.809
Really?


00:14:47.851 --> 00:14:49.822
So, you two are...?


00:14:54.702 --> 00:14:56.726
No, not yet.


00:14:56.736 --> 00:14:59.709
But, we're planning on spending
some time together
in London.


00:14:59.740 --> 00:15:01.938
Really?
Why didn't you tell me?


00:15:01.949 --> 00:15:03.774
Hey, wait...
where are you going?


00:15:03.815 --> 00:15:06.746
Ah, some details, please...


00:15:07.924 --> 00:15:10.793
I really needed someone
to talk to today.


00:15:10.835 --> 00:15:11.962
Thank you.


00:15:12.973 --> 00:15:14.902
I'm going to call you
from London.


00:15:15.736 --> 00:15:17.728
Really?
- Really.


00:15:18.739 --> 00:15:21.722
I'm gonna make sure you
won't forget about me, right?
- Right, right.


00:15:21.754 --> 00:15:25.727
I'm sure you've got a girl at every airport.
Do you call all of them?


00:15:25.758 --> 00:15:26.749
None of them, actually.


00:15:26.759 --> 00:15:27.970
Chloe.


00:15:28.867 --> 00:15:29.899
Oh, hi, Jim.


00:15:29.941 --> 00:15:32.733
I got these things for your dad.


00:15:32.733 --> 00:15:33.943
They're for tomorrow night.


00:15:36.749 --> 00:15:39.012
U2. Wow.


00:15:39.022 --> 00:15:40.983
These can't be easy to get.


00:15:41.024 --> 00:15:44.727
You're telling me.
It took me two weeks to find these things.


00:15:45.801 --> 00:15:47.773
Two weeks?


00:15:52.820 --> 00:15:54.885
Chloe, I'm sorry...


00:15:57.022 --> 00:15:58.785
Mr. Williams, please.


00:15:58.827 --> 00:16:00.767
I'm coming, sorry.


00:16:00.966 --> 00:16:02.830
Chloe, I ..


00:16:06.877 --> 00:16:08.941
Would you give these to my dad, please?


00:16:09.921 --> 00:16:11.747
Of course.


00:16:13.927 --> 00:16:15.867
Well, you...


00:16:18.035 --> 00:16:20.767
Excuse me...
- Thanks.


00:16:24.950 --> 00:16:28.016
Mr. Williams, please...
- Sorry.


00:16:41.885 --> 00:16:43.939
Excuse me, Captain.


00:16:44.993 --> 00:16:47.829
Chloe asked me to
give you these.


00:16:49.968 --> 00:16:53.065
You are the GWN guy, right?


00:16:53.107 --> 00:16:55.881
GWN guy...
Yeah, that's me.


00:16:55.912 --> 00:16:58.894
Cameron Williams, Chris Smith...
Hi, pleased to meet you.


00:16:58.894 --> 00:17:00.051
Pleased to meet you.


00:18:05.157 --> 00:18:08.961
Welcome aboard
Pancon flight 257 to London.


00:18:08.992 --> 00:18:11.934
Flight time today will be
6 hours and 30 minutes.


00:18:11.965 --> 00:18:14.123
Thank you and enjoy Your flight.


00:18:15.083 --> 00:18:17.941
So, did you get her number?


00:18:19.954 --> 00:18:25.992
Come on... I saw you two at the lounge
about an hour ago and you happened to be
the last person to get on the plane.


00:18:26.201 --> 00:18:30.133
And to think, I could have spend
the last time with you instead.


00:18:32.176 --> 00:18:36.171
I do not know why you uncaring guys
always wanted to get the girls.
.


00:18:36.181 --> 00:18:40.121
Maybe because we do not want to go around
like a dress rehearsal for Glee.


00:18:42.031 --> 00:18:44.127
You know what, I'm must say
right on that one.


00:18:44.168 --> 00:18:47.932
I will have to thank you though
for flying first class.


00:18:47.943 --> 00:18:49.967
No need to thank, man.


00:18:49.977 --> 00:18:52.177
But, that guy who's sitting tight
back there...


00:18:52.219 --> 00:18:53.982
Now, you should.


00:19:03.065 --> 00:19:05.130
I know you!


00:19:05.182 --> 00:19:09.019
Look, George. It's Frank Sinatra!


00:19:09.060 --> 00:19:11.114
What's that?
- It is Frank...


00:19:11.156 --> 00:19:12.220
Oh!


00:19:12.230 --> 00:19:14.191
Listen , George.


00:19:14.233 --> 00:19:16.965
We're home!


00:19:18.280 --> 00:19:21.242
Oh...we're not home.


00:19:23.056 --> 00:19:26.247
Sometimes he gets a bit confused.


00:19:31.129 --> 00:19:38.136
Good afternoon, this is your Captain Rayford Steele
on flight Pancon 257, weather conditions
are reported to be good.


00:19:38.147 --> 00:19:44.184
So, will be a nice smooth flight all the way to London.
Please sit back and enjoy our excellent service.


00:19:45.195 --> 00:19:50.190
We will be serving complimentary
drinks and snacks shortly.
So, please sit back and relax.


00:19:51.066 --> 00:19:55.030
No Johnny, you don't have to tell them anything.
Just do what you do best.


00:19:55.040 --> 00:20:00.182
Stall 'em! But if you see one thing that
makes you think they smell an acquisition...


00:20:00.224 --> 00:20:03.091
Dish it all.


00:20:03.091 --> 00:20:04.227
Look!


00:20:04.269 --> 00:20:11.234
I left the company jet in Houston.
I'll be in London and with the paper signed
before they know that I'm gone.


00:20:11.245 --> 00:20:14.248
We'll go and get.
Good!


00:20:42.310 --> 00:20:45.148
Chloe, Chloe!


00:20:45.189 --> 00:20:47.046
Hey! Come here!


00:20:47.088 --> 00:20:49.080
Oh God, Oh my goodness!


00:20:49.121 --> 00:20:51.154
You are so big!


00:20:51.196 --> 00:20:53.063
Ok.


00:20:53.293 --> 00:20:55.201
Did you get me anything
at the airport?


00:20:55.232 --> 00:20:58.215
Well, you'll just have to
wait and see.


00:20:59.081 --> 00:21:02.074
Alright, check it out in there
and see what you've got.


00:21:02.116 --> 00:21:05.182
The new baseball gloves that
I've been asking for!


00:21:05.192 --> 00:21:07.184
No way! Mom!


00:21:07.225 --> 00:21:09.353
Chloe is here!


00:21:12.274 --> 00:21:14.232
Mom, Chloe is here!


00:21:16.213 --> 00:21:18.154
She is here, mom!


00:21:19.353 --> 00:21:22.117
Hi!
- Hey...


00:21:22.127 --> 00:21:24.193
My Gosh...


00:21:25.100 --> 00:21:27.331
Oh, you look beautiful.


00:21:27.373 --> 00:21:29.271
Wow.


00:21:29.271 --> 00:21:31.137
So,


00:21:32.150 --> 00:21:34.235
Um, can I get you
something to drink?


00:21:34.278 --> 00:21:36.081
Yeah... Yeah...
Sure.


00:21:36.123 --> 00:21:39.116
Mom... mom... Chloe got me a brand new
baseball gloves. See?


00:21:52.192 --> 00:21:55.248
6 hours to London.
Nobody laughing at that too.


00:21:55.290 --> 00:21:58.136
The Hyperjet...
that'll change everything.


00:21:58.136 --> 00:21:59.326
Oh yeah?
Why is that?


00:21:59.336 --> 00:22:01.359
The Defence Deartment.


00:22:04.207 --> 00:22:07.272
Did you say the Defence Department?
- Yeah.


00:22:07.283 --> 00:22:12.133
It seems that they've been
developing a new jet, ok?
It'll carry 300 passengers at Mach 40...


00:22:12.164 --> 00:22:14.260
New York to London...6 minutes.


00:22:14.260 --> 00:22:17.178
6 minutes?
- 6 minutes.


00:22:17.199 --> 00:22:20.265
That's pretty fast.
- Personally, I think they're lying.


00:22:20.307 --> 00:22:22.298
Yeah, I think that's
a good guess.


00:22:22.319 --> 00:22:25.438
There's no way they can develop themselves.
I'm guessing they...


00:22:25.448 --> 00:22:28.181
...referred engineering
from something else.


00:22:28.223 --> 00:22:30.319
Probably something from Area 51.


00:22:31.403 --> 00:22:33.165
Yeah.


00:22:33.436 --> 00:22:35.345
Scotch, please!


00:22:35.345 --> 00:22:39.434
So, was your dad surprised?


00:22:41.185 --> 00:22:43.387
Yeah. I think he was.


00:22:43.397 --> 00:22:46.158
Must have meant
a lot to him.


00:22:46.189 --> 00:22:48.254
He seemed very upset that
he had to leave.


00:22:49.266 --> 00:22:51.301
Yeah, I could tell.


00:22:52.239 --> 00:22:53.438
So, how was your flight?


00:22:53.480 --> 00:22:56.274
Good.
Yeah, it was good.


00:22:57.213 --> 00:22:58.350
School?


00:22:58.361 --> 00:23:00.331
It's fine.


00:23:01.490 --> 00:23:05.265
Hey, you'll eh...
you'll never guess who I met
at the airport.


00:23:05.307 --> 00:23:06.496
Buck Williams.


00:23:07.340 --> 00:23:09.467
Sorry, Cameron Williams.


00:23:09.478 --> 00:23:11.407
From the news?
- Yeah!


00:23:11.448 --> 00:23:13.316
Really?
- Hm-hmm.


00:23:13.326 --> 00:23:15.350
Did you get a chance
to talk to him?


00:23:15.360 --> 00:23:17.329
I did... actually.


00:23:17.329 --> 00:23:19.456
Erm, he is...


00:23:19.498 --> 00:23:21.470
He is a great guy.


00:23:21.470 --> 00:23:25.275
Hmm, so just happens
to be gorgeous.


00:23:25.317 --> 00:23:27.278
Yes...


00:23:27.320 --> 00:23:28.374
I told him that you were a fan.


00:23:28.416 --> 00:23:29.479
Oh!


00:23:29.490 --> 00:23:36.331
By the way, you're not the only one who thinks
every earthquake will be the end of the world.


00:23:36.373 --> 00:23:39.502
Some crazy lady cornered him
at the airport.


00:23:44.414 --> 00:23:47.364
That's not how
I learnt that .


00:23:49.490 --> 00:23:51.482
Anyway, Hmm...


00:23:52.401 --> 00:23:55.268
He is a great guy.


00:23:59.283 --> 00:24:00.410
Chloe, honey...


00:24:01.411 --> 00:24:03.518
I don't mean to push.


00:24:03.559 --> 00:24:06.458
I know it must feel that way.


00:24:07.502 --> 00:24:11.308
I just want you to understand.


00:24:11.474 --> 00:24:13.445
It's important to me.


00:24:13.476 --> 00:24:15.375
So are you.


00:24:16.325 --> 00:24:17.514
I just want you to be ready.


00:24:17.555 --> 00:24:19.451
Ready for what?


00:24:20.494 --> 00:24:21.557
You know...


00:24:21.557 --> 00:24:23.425
Never mind.


00:24:24.530 --> 00:24:27.303
Can we just talk without
you cutting me off?


00:24:27.303 --> 00:24:29.359
Mom, I just got here.


00:24:29.411 --> 00:24:32.373
I'm not really up for a
heavy conversation.


00:24:33.416 --> 00:24:36.325
Ok, sure...
But just hear me out.


00:24:36.325 --> 00:24:37.555
Just a little.


00:24:38.463 --> 00:24:44.303
I've been praying for you to come home
and I believe that's why God
brought you here.


00:24:44.335 --> 00:24:45.575
What did you say?


00:24:45.607 --> 00:24:48.308
God brought me home?


00:24:48.319 --> 00:24:51.372
God did not bring me home,
I brought me home.


00:24:51.413 --> 00:24:53.552
I bought the ticket,
I got on on the flight.


00:24:53.584 --> 00:24:56.389
God had nothing to do with it.


00:24:56.399 --> 00:24:57.588
And let me ask you something.


00:24:57.599 --> 00:25:00.403
If God brought me home
for dad's birthday...


00:25:00.435 --> 00:25:02.594
Then why did He let him
fly off to London?


00:25:04.346 --> 00:25:06.682
Maybe it's important
for us to talk.


00:25:06.787 --> 00:25:07.756
I don't think so.


00:25:08.351 --> 00:25:13.388
One thing I do know for sure,
God is the reason dad is not here
right now.


00:25:18.614 --> 00:25:20.480
Chloe!


00:25:27.496 --> 00:25:29.467
I'll be right back.
- Yeah.


00:25:44.590 --> 00:25:46.529
Can I give you a hand
with your bag?


00:25:46.529 --> 00:25:48.595
Did I ask for a hand?


00:25:49.481 --> 00:25:51.525
I, I can put it on the top
for you.


00:25:51.535 --> 00:25:53.483
Yeah?
So could I!


00:26:04.633 --> 00:26:06.603
What are you looking at?


00:26:07.480 --> 00:26:09.513
Want to ask me
a question?


00:26:09.680 --> 00:26:12.455
Wonder how I drive?


00:26:12.653 --> 00:26:15.458
Maybe, where I buy
my clothes?


00:26:15.697 --> 00:26:18.461
How do I reach the urinal?


00:26:18.471 --> 00:26:20.527
What is a urinal?


00:26:24.508 --> 00:26:26.500
That's my dad.


00:26:26.510 --> 00:26:28.576
He plays football.


00:26:28.586 --> 00:26:30.578
That's nice, kid.


00:26:30.661 --> 00:26:34.594
He's going to be on TV tomorrow
if his arm felt better.


00:26:35.564 --> 00:26:37.597
Your dad plays ball on TV?


00:26:38.473 --> 00:26:39.526
What team?


00:26:39.609 --> 00:26:42.446
Gooo...Jets!


00:26:43.583 --> 00:26:46.556
Oh. What's wrong with his arm?


00:26:46.556 --> 00:26:48.620
Cosmo.
He's my dog.


00:26:48.631 --> 00:26:50.602
He knocked daddy off
the hammock.


00:26:50.634 --> 00:26:52.531
Oh, really?


00:26:52.531 --> 00:26:55.709
Daddy was so mad.
He pushed Cosmo onto the floor.


00:26:55.741 --> 00:26:58.579
What did I tell you about
bothering other passengers?


00:26:58.579 --> 00:26:59.642
Sorry...


00:27:08.631 --> 00:27:11.573
So, you're a bad man.


00:27:11.604 --> 00:27:13.503
Yup.


00:27:13.513 --> 00:27:15.713
You're gonna give
the kid a cut?


00:27:16.714 --> 00:27:21.522
Her dad's PK Carvell.
Doubt she needs the money.


00:27:26.536 --> 00:27:27.704
Where are you going?


00:27:27.704 --> 00:27:30.468
Out!
- Can I come?


00:27:30.510 --> 00:27:31.678
Raymie, not now!


00:27:31.709 --> 00:27:33.690
Please.


00:27:36.487 --> 00:27:39.552
Alright, get your stuff.
- Awesome!


00:27:59.647 --> 00:28:03.672
Can we go to the mall?
- Yes, we can.


00:28:03.714 --> 00:28:08.522
I heard there's 80% off
for Games stuff.


00:28:18.575 --> 00:28:20.546
Do you think
mom is crazy?


00:28:20.588 --> 00:28:21.610
What?


00:28:22.590 --> 00:28:23.748
No.


00:28:23.791 --> 00:28:26.627
No, I was just upset.


00:28:29.701 --> 00:28:33.695
Dad says pastor Bruce
was washing her brains.


00:28:33.706 --> 00:28:35.770
Oh, that's just a joke.


00:28:36.616 --> 00:28:37.773
It is?


00:28:39.682 --> 00:28:40.850
I don't get it.


00:28:41.862 --> 00:28:44.562
Neither do I..


00:29:06.639 --> 00:29:08.703
So this is kinda sucked.


00:29:09.747 --> 00:29:13.596
What is that?
- Got to fly on your birthday?


00:29:13.627 --> 00:29:15.723
Well, you have gotta
pay the bills, right?


00:29:16.599 --> 00:29:18.622
So how long is Chloe
going to be in town?


00:29:20.927 --> 00:29:22.887
Well, looks like smooth sailing.


00:29:22.897 --> 00:29:26.841
I wanna stretch my legs and see
how's the crew is doing.


00:30:36.146 --> 00:30:39.910
Raymie, what are you trying to do?
Scare me to death!


00:30:40.954 --> 00:30:42.048
What was that?


00:30:43.092 --> 00:30:45.063
Come on.
- Can I have it?


00:30:45.094 --> 00:30:47.190
No you can't.
- Only a few hundred dollars.


00:30:47.200 --> 00:30:48.931
NO!


00:31:02.133 --> 00:31:03.999
I got 'em.


00:31:12.009 --> 00:31:16.014
I'm going to find a way
to pay you back.


00:31:18.934 --> 00:31:21.134
What's wrong?
- No...


00:31:21.176 --> 00:31:25.202
I just thought the seats should be
a liitle closer to the stage.


00:31:26.109 --> 00:31:28.080
Coffee?
- Uhuh..


00:31:52.033 --> 00:31:53.233
She'll be ok.


00:31:54.005 --> 00:31:54.997
Huh?


00:31:55.007 --> 00:31:56.978
Mom.


00:32:00.085 --> 00:32:03.224
She still wears that necklace, you know.
The one you made her.


00:32:04.027 --> 00:32:06.152
She never takes it off.


00:32:09.262 --> 00:32:13.005
They're gonna be alright, right?
Mom and dad?


00:32:13.005 --> 00:32:15.215
Hmm? Yes, yes of course.


00:32:15.247 --> 00:32:19.085
Dad's being called in to work,
he's got something to do, ok?


00:32:19.251 --> 00:32:21.223
Did dad tell you about
my game?


00:32:21.223 --> 00:32:23.027
Are you kidding me?


00:32:23.100 --> 00:32:24.999
You're all we talk about.


00:32:25.072 --> 00:32:28.231
He said that you were the greatest baseball
player in the whole world.


00:32:28.273 --> 00:32:30.202
And you know what?
- What?


00:32:30.243 --> 00:32:32.112
He is right.


00:32:35.021 --> 00:32:36.082
I love you.


00:32:36.124 --> 00:32:37.094
I miss you, buddy.


00:33:04.251 --> 00:33:05.305
No, it is not possible.


00:33:08.055 --> 00:33:10.049
Allahu Akbar!


00:33:19.152 --> 00:33:20.143
Kathy?


00:33:20.435 --> 00:33:23.283
Do you see my daughter?


00:33:36.434 --> 00:33:38.309
Chris! Let me in!


00:33:41.250 --> 00:33:42.272
Do you hear me?


00:34:19.324 --> 00:34:20.451
Raymie!


00:34:31.578 --> 00:34:33.309
Where is he?


00:34:33.319 --> 00:34:34.519
Everyone sit.


00:35:20.549 --> 00:35:22.489
Everyone sit down!


00:35:26.494 --> 00:35:28.486
Sit down! Everyone sit down!


00:35:30.374 --> 00:35:31.563
Hey, what's going on?


00:35:31.573 --> 00:35:33.565
What happened?


00:35:37.517 --> 00:35:39.385
Let's go!
I want some answers.


00:35:39.520 --> 00:35:41.353
I want to see the captain!


00:35:41.395 --> 00:35:43.585
Hey, I want to see your captain.


00:35:44.398 --> 00:35:46.599
Hey, I want to see the captain!


00:35:46.641 --> 00:35:48.372
No!


00:35:52.418 --> 00:35:54.546
Attention, this is the captain.


00:35:54.619 --> 00:36:00.531
This is the captain.
All passengers take your seats
immediately.


00:36:01.565 --> 00:36:03.557
Hey, back off!
- I want to see the captain!


00:36:04.537 --> 00:36:05.601
Tell us what just happened?


00:36:15.632 --> 00:36:17.499
We are experiencing a
decompression.


00:36:17.530 --> 00:36:20.471
Please go to your seats,
and put on your oxygen masks.


00:36:29.627 --> 00:36:31.452
This is so crazy.


00:37:19.558 --> 00:37:20.685
Come on!


00:37:28.745 --> 00:37:30.717
Stop it! Stop it!


00:37:39.737 --> 00:37:41.605
Stop!


00:37:59.583 --> 00:38:02.711
This is Pancon 257.
We have an emergency.


00:38:05.590 --> 00:38:09.595
This is Pancon 257.
We have an emergency.


00:38:11.628 --> 00:38:16.632
Mayday! Mayday! This is
Pancon heavy 257. Acknowledge!


00:38:26.602 --> 00:38:28.834
Drop the pressure,
it's ok now...


00:38:30.575 --> 00:38:31.806
Everyone on this plane
is scared to death.


00:38:31.848 --> 00:38:34.779
I really need you
to step up your hand.


00:38:34.820 --> 00:38:37.647
Can you do it?
- Yeah


00:38:37.689 --> 00:38:40.660
I'm going to say something to the passengers,
watch the flight deck.


00:39:04.708 --> 00:39:06.815
Hello. I'm Captain Steele!


00:39:06.815 --> 00:39:13.750
I need you to remain in your seats with
your seat belts fastened.
But you can now all remove your oxygen masks.


00:39:13.896 --> 00:39:15.701
What's going on?


00:39:15.774 --> 00:39:18.597
My kid...
Where is my kid?


00:39:18.597 --> 00:39:21.664
I know you all want answers,
and believe me, so do I.


00:39:21.716 --> 00:39:24.647
And I'll do my best to get them.
But, right now...


00:39:24.647 --> 00:39:26.753
I have to do my job so that
we're all safe.


00:39:26.795 --> 00:39:28.651
Safe? Safe from what?


00:39:28.693 --> 00:39:30.758
Sit down!


00:39:33.834 --> 00:39:36.640
Safe from our own panic.


00:39:36.713 --> 00:39:38.830
It is the biggest threat on
this plane right now.
.


00:39:38.883 --> 00:39:42.720
Now, I'm going to ask the flight attendants
to do a head count.


00:39:42.720 --> 00:39:45.692
Whatever happened to those people,
we will find them.


00:39:45.734 --> 00:39:49.695
I haven't been able to reach anyone yet.
So, I... I don't know if...


00:39:49.904 --> 00:39:56.641
This event was isolated to our aircraft
or others in the area have been affected,
but I promise...


00:39:56.651 --> 00:39:57.881
As soon as I have something
to tell you...


00:39:57.881 --> 00:39:58.810
I will.


00:39:58.852 --> 00:40:00.718
That's it?


00:40:13.922 --> 00:40:15.778
Raymie?


00:40:41.807 --> 00:40:43.799
Kimmy...


00:40:46.750 --> 00:40:49.890
Oh God .. Kimmy...


00:41:02.747 --> 00:41:03.769
Kimmy is gone.


00:41:03.884 --> 00:41:05.751
Ray, what is happening?
Hattie...


00:41:05.959 --> 00:41:10.828
Hattie... you've gotta pull yourself together.
- Just hold me... just hold me.


00:41:10.871 --> 00:41:12.894
Hattie... look at me,
look at me.


00:41:13.844 --> 00:41:16.815
We're trained for emergencies.
We're going to do our jobs.


00:41:16.847 --> 00:41:18.777
I really need to manage things here?


00:41:18.787 --> 00:41:21.978
So, I really need you to focus.
Alright?


00:41:22.019 --> 00:41:23.967
Ok?
- Ok.


00:41:24.791 --> 00:41:25.856
Now listen...


00:41:25.970 --> 00:41:28.964
I want to go back and do full check
on the manifest.


00:41:29.808 --> 00:41:30.997
At least, find out who they are.


00:41:31.039 --> 00:41:33.948
And how many of them
are missing, right?
-Ok.


00:41:36.920 --> 00:41:37.890
Ray...


00:41:37.932 --> 00:41:39.017
I'm scared.


00:41:40.759 --> 00:41:41.791
Aren't you?


00:41:42.000 --> 00:41:45.806
I will be.
As soon as I have time.


00:42:25.922 --> 00:42:32.837
Please, please help me, no one knows
where my baby has gone.


00:42:32.837 --> 00:42:35.965
I'm sorry...


00:42:44.863 --> 00:42:48.992
This is Cameron Williams,
reporting from flight 257.


00:42:50.107 --> 00:42:54.051
We are somewhere over the Atlantic,
heading for London.


00:42:55.020 --> 00:42:56.760
Abbout 3 hours
from JFK Airport.


00:42:56.895 --> 00:43:02.954
Something impossible just took place
on this plane.


00:43:05.875 --> 00:43:07.961
Ma'am, can you tell me what you saw?


00:43:08.013 --> 00:43:10.036
I don't know.


00:43:10.078 --> 00:43:13.946
My Kids gone... disappeared


00:43:13.988 --> 00:43:15.115
Do you know when
it happened?


00:43:15.866 --> 00:43:16.950
Nothing!


00:43:16.992 --> 00:43:23.959
I was sitting here, I thought maybe I was
holding it and dropping something but...


00:43:24.011 --> 00:43:28.910
Neighbour was sreaming.
I don't know.


00:43:45.086 --> 00:43:51.051
As unbelievable this may sound,
people from over this plane
simply vanished.


00:43:53.168 --> 00:43:58.871
Leaving their clothes and
personal possessions
and everything else...


00:44:12.043 --> 00:44:13.941
Hey!


00:44:15.182 --> 00:44:18.019
That's my brother's!


00:44:22.097 --> 00:44:24.088
No!


00:44:59.971 --> 00:45:01.202
Are you okay?


00:45:07.991 --> 00:45:12.122
Isn't it? It can't be...


00:45:12.132 --> 00:45:14.124
This is what?


00:45:15.010 --> 00:45:17.054
No...


00:45:17.106 --> 00:45:19.171
I know what's going on here.


00:45:19.213 --> 00:45:21.142
What do you know?


00:45:35.147 --> 00:45:37.076
Okay.


00:45:39.182 --> 00:45:42.050
It's a bad trip.


00:45:43.125 --> 00:45:45.148
You must move on.


00:45:46.065 --> 00:45:49.038
It's not going to last forever.


00:45:54.252 --> 00:45:58.090
Hello? Can anyone hear me?


00:46:18.237 --> 00:46:20.260
Hey, hey.


00:46:20.302 --> 00:46:22.211
It's alright.


00:46:23.107 --> 00:46:25.204
Let's go back to
your seat.


00:46:30.085 --> 00:46:32.150
Buckle in... alright.


00:46:35.130 --> 00:46:38.239
You're safe.
But you knew what happened.


00:46:42.243 --> 00:46:45.226
None of this is happening.


00:46:46.123 --> 00:46:49.220
That's okay,
we'll going to get through this.


00:46:51.264 --> 00:46:53.361
Alright...
None of this is happening.


00:46:55.144 --> 00:46:59.210
Why don't you relax, ok?
Sit back and relax.


00:47:00.150 --> 00:47:02.278
Try get some sleep.


00:47:06.332 --> 00:47:08.356
Can you tell me what you saw?


00:47:08.408 --> 00:47:13.101
It was the same thing you did.
Doesn't look any different from
down here.


00:47:13.111 --> 00:47:15.176
Oh, come on...


00:47:15.280 --> 00:47:21.245
Anything strange before
the people vanished?
Flash or sound... anything.


00:47:22.205 --> 00:47:24.103
No.


00:47:24.301 --> 00:47:26.231
What about there?


00:47:26.231 --> 00:47:28.212
Who was that?


00:47:28.379 --> 00:47:31.248
I do not know, some guy!


00:47:31.248 --> 00:47:34.313
Anything unusual about that guy?


00:47:34.428 --> 00:47:39.162
Look, pal, there's something
unusual about all of us here.


00:47:39.297 --> 00:47:42.175
Get that thing off my face.


00:47:53.167 --> 00:47:57.255
Hi, this is the Steele's household.
Please leave your name and number.


00:47:57.370 --> 00:47:59.132
Mom...


00:47:59.174 --> 00:48:02.303
Mom, please pick up the phone.
I do not know what's going on.


00:48:04.441 --> 00:48:09.288
Raymie, if you went home and
you can hear me right now.


00:48:09.330 --> 00:48:11.385
I need you to listen, ok?


00:48:11.426 --> 00:48:14.367
I know that you are scared
and I'm too scared.


00:48:14.409 --> 00:48:17.235
But I really need you
to pick up the phone.


00:48:17.235 --> 00:48:20.177
Need you to let me know
that you're okay.


00:48:20.208 --> 00:48:22.377
I need to hear your voice.


00:48:26.361 --> 00:48:29.198
I love you guys.


00:48:47.435 --> 00:48:51.169
I think, we should all be
doing right now...


00:48:51.211 --> 00:48:52.380
Is saying a prayer.


00:48:52.411 --> 00:48:54.392
A prayer?


00:48:57.261 --> 00:48:59.283
A prayer to who?


00:48:59.429 --> 00:49:01.369
To God.


00:49:01.463 --> 00:49:03.454
Whose God?


00:49:04.310 --> 00:49:06.376
Yours or mine?


00:49:06.407 --> 00:49:08.396
Just Allah.


00:49:11.253 --> 00:49:13.277
You know what I think?


00:49:13.288 --> 00:49:15.258
No.


00:49:16.228 --> 00:49:19.326
Attention passengers...
Since we haven't reached the halfway point
I'm turning back to New York.


00:49:19.378 --> 00:49:22.434
We'll be over JFK inside of 3 hours.


00:49:42.414 --> 00:49:44.281
...


00:49:46.419 --> 00:49:50.298
Raymie! Raymie
- Back off.


00:49:57.380 --> 00:50:00.352
Hi, this is Irene Steele...


00:50:07.465 --> 00:50:09.405
You okay?


00:50:10.435 --> 00:50:12.343
Did you do the count?


00:50:12.374 --> 00:50:15.441
I tried. But many of them are
not in their seats.


00:50:15.451 --> 00:50:19.258
Maybe they're not there at all.
They're scared, Ray.


00:50:19.300 --> 00:50:21.260
We're all scared.


00:50:21.333 --> 00:50:26.433
Well, Let's hope whatever it was
doesn't happen again.


00:50:26.475 --> 00:50:28.445
What is that?


00:50:29.479 --> 00:50:34.443
Charlie 1581, this is Pancon
257, do you copy?


00:50:35.465 --> 00:50:40.397
Charlie 1581, we have an emergency situation.
Repeat, we have an...


00:51:03.413 --> 00:51:06.551
You are approaching our flight path!
Get out there and prep the cabin!


00:51:06.624 --> 00:51:08.554
Now!


00:51:14.569 --> 00:51:19.607
All passengers, take your seats
and put seat belts on immediately!


00:51:29.566 --> 00:51:37.493
Charlie 1581, you're in our airspace.
I'm climbing 1,000 feet.
That is one, zero, zero, zero feet.


00:52:15.503 --> 00:52:16.691
Damn!


00:52:17.525 --> 00:52:18.632
Mayday!


00:52:18.673 --> 00:52:21.499
This is Pancon 257.


00:52:21.541 --> 00:52:24.513
We have been involved in a collision.


00:52:24.576 --> 00:52:27.549
Charlie 1581 is down.


00:52:27.549 --> 00:52:29.686
Our Coordinates are...


00:52:31.667 --> 00:52:38.478
4-7...
This is an emergency situation.


00:52:42.692 --> 00:52:45.557
We have a plane down,
It's search and rescue...


00:52:45.588 --> 00:52:49.490
Repeat, this is an emergency.


00:52:50.710 --> 00:52:54.609
Come on, there has to be
someone out there.


00:54:13.605 --> 00:54:15.599
What is wrong with you?


00:54:15.651 --> 00:54:19.778
You really believe a group of terrorists
could develop a bomb like this?


00:54:20.789 --> 00:54:22.750
We are not talking about
a car bomb.


00:54:22.761 --> 00:54:25.691
If this was a weapon,
it is not from this planet.


00:54:25.764 --> 00:54:27.631
What exactly are you saying?


00:54:27.642 --> 00:54:30.656
I'm just saying,
maybe they were abducted.


00:54:30.708 --> 00:54:32.700
Aliens?


00:54:32.814 --> 00:54:34.743
Come on.


00:54:34.785 --> 00:54:36.850
Can you believe this guy?


00:55:11.692 --> 00:55:12.860
Is everything okay?


00:55:12.891 --> 00:55:14.653
That other plane,
did it lose people?


00:55:14.695 --> 00:55:15.863
I don't know.


00:55:18.868 --> 00:55:23.641
Your camera, I need you to take
a picture of the wing for the captain.


00:55:50.632 --> 00:55:51.798
Raymie!


00:55:52.778 --> 00:55:54.708
Raymie!


00:57:03.754 --> 00:57:05.747
Be careful.


00:57:10.899 --> 00:57:12.870
Okay.


00:57:12.870 --> 00:57:14.810
Here's what I can get.


00:57:14.841 --> 00:57:16.812
Looks like we came about...


00:57:16.812 --> 00:57:19.012
6 inches from losing a wing.


00:57:19.022 --> 00:57:20.994
And the spoiler is gone.


00:57:21.025 --> 00:57:22.965
What does that mean?


00:57:22.997 --> 00:57:26.790
It's just gonna be a lot tougher
to slow down when we get home.


00:57:26.801 --> 00:57:30.899
One thing the runway at JFK is long enough.
Good thing we didn't hit the tail.


00:57:31.838 --> 00:57:34.842
I guess it's our
lucky day.


00:58:19.006 --> 00:58:21.843
They're all gone.


00:58:23.993 --> 00:58:28.015
Not just the babies.
The older kids too.


00:58:28.933 --> 00:58:30.925
Are you sure?


00:58:30.936 --> 00:58:33.866
I'm looking for my brother.


00:58:34.001 --> 00:58:38.039
I heard some doctors
talking a while ago.


00:58:39.978 --> 00:58:42.074
This is not just here.


00:58:42.126 --> 00:58:45.118
It's everywhere.


00:58:45.129 --> 00:58:48.102
All over the world.


00:58:49.906 --> 00:58:54.850
They say no one has seen a single kid
since it happened.


00:59:01.961 --> 00:59:05.902
We either damaged some
of our computer sensors or...


00:59:05.944 --> 00:59:14.006
Cameron, I lost the auto-pilot
Can you go to the very back and see there's
anything liquid spilling out from the wing?


00:59:14.016 --> 00:59:16.050
Liquid?


00:59:16.091 --> 00:59:17.959
You mean fuel?


00:59:17.959 --> 00:59:22.953
I want to take us up to a few thousand feet,
enter a small range, just in case.


00:59:35.060 --> 00:59:37.124
Perfect.


00:59:48.951 --> 00:59:50.923
We have to go back.
We have to go back.


00:59:50.965 --> 00:59:56.169
We are going back. We're only just a few...
- No, I mean, back to where they disappeared.
I need to find my baby.


00:59:56.169 --> 00:59:59.120
We are losing fuel. We have a little left.
We're not gonna have enough to get home.


00:59:59.151 --> 01:00:04.886
What? We can't get home?!!
- We have fuel reserves.
We'll gonna be fine.


01:00:10.203 --> 01:00:13.040
Are we on fire?!!!


01:00:16.086 --> 01:00:18.057
We have the right to know
if we're going to die, ok?!!


01:00:18.057 --> 01:00:20.122
No one is going to die!


01:00:20.154 --> 01:00:22.958
Hey, everyone, listen up!


01:00:22.990 --> 01:00:26.953
No one is going to die, you hear me?
- Everyone sit down, Everyone sit!


01:00:26.974 --> 01:00:29.029
Now, captain's right.


01:00:29.112 --> 01:00:33.208
As hard as it may be,
we all need to stay calm.


01:01:04.013 --> 01:01:06.246
We're on fire.
- Where?


01:01:06.246 --> 01:01:08.978
The wing on this side.
- Is the wing on fire or is the spray on fire?


01:01:09.020 --> 01:01:11.116
The spray. It's big.


01:01:12.190 --> 01:01:14.224
We'll fly afront of it.
It'll burn off.


01:01:14.266 --> 01:01:19.011
But?
- It's fuel.


01:01:19.042 --> 01:01:20.241
Fuel that we need to hang on.


01:01:20.252 --> 01:01:24.184
Are you still going to get us back?
- Well, that depends.


01:01:24.184 --> 01:01:29.064
If the leak is here
or here.


01:01:30.306 --> 01:01:32.131
So what do we do?


01:01:32.131 --> 01:01:36.049
Let it burn.
See what is left.


01:02:02.196 --> 01:02:04.185
Fire is out.


01:02:05.040 --> 01:02:07.064
Levels haven't change.


01:02:07.106 --> 01:02:10.172
Does it mean we'll empty?
- Means we don't know.


01:02:11.152 --> 01:02:14.061
And we've lost the elevators.
- The what?


01:02:14.082 --> 01:02:21.091
The elevators. Can't climb. Looks like
we begun our decend at New York 2 hours early.


01:02:25.179 --> 01:02:27.077
Can't believe we can't reach anyone.


01:02:27.119 --> 01:02:29.110
You have a satellite phone?


01:02:29.121 --> 01:02:31.113
Investigative journalist.


01:02:31.322 --> 01:02:34.159
Pilot.


01:02:35.200 --> 01:02:38.171
Yes, the only other plane was
the one that nearly hit us.


01:02:38.203 --> 01:02:41.238
Did you talk to them?
Did they lose any passengers?


01:02:41.248 --> 01:02:43.302
I don't know about passengers.


01:02:43.313 --> 01:02:46.119
But I do know this.


01:02:47.089 --> 01:02:50.290
There wasn't anyone
flying that plane.


01:03:38.260 --> 01:03:41.201
Excuse me. I was just thinking...


01:03:43.245 --> 01:03:45.299
What if they are still here?


01:03:46.249 --> 01:03:48.147
What?


01:03:48.283 --> 01:03:51.151
I mean ..


01:03:51.359 --> 01:03:53.288
What if we just cannot see them?


01:03:53.319 --> 01:03:57.356
Like, you know,
if they're invisible.


01:03:59.213 --> 01:04:00.328
Jeez wheez.


01:04:00.370 --> 01:04:04.177
Isn't invisible any crazier
than vanished?


01:05:01.408 --> 01:05:07.279
Hello, this is to restore alarm.
We have detected an alarm at your premise.


01:05:07.310 --> 01:05:10.342
Due to unusual call volume...


01:05:19.468 --> 01:05:22.378
(Pray)


01:05:53.507 --> 01:05:55.269
What do you know
about Kimmy?


01:05:55.311 --> 01:05:56.437
What?


01:05:56.437 --> 01:05:58.314
How well did you know her?


01:05:58.356 --> 01:06:01.328
Not very. She's just a friend.


01:06:01.328 --> 01:06:03.352
Go through her stuff.
- What stuff?


01:06:03.363 --> 01:06:08.400
Anything. Her purse, her jacket, her ID badge.
Just go get her things and bring them in here.


01:06:08.504 --> 01:06:10.527
Please
- OK


01:08:03.538 --> 01:08:06.407
We have another aircraft in our area.


01:08:06.448 --> 01:08:17.490
Please fasten your seat belts, Charlie 1581 you're in
our airspace. We are climbing 1,000 feet
That is one, zero, zero, zero...


01:09:17.518 --> 01:09:22.628
Dump the purse. Dump the purse.
Come on, just...


01:09:24.504 --> 01:09:26.673
What are you looking for?


01:09:46.656 --> 01:09:51.523
Either I'm going crazy, or the
world is going insane.


01:09:51.555 --> 01:09:54.527
What are you talking about?


01:09:58.710 --> 01:10:01.734
I think I know where they are.


01:10:06.698 --> 01:10:08.815
What if we are now where
we think we are or even went?


01:10:08.826 --> 01:10:10.525
What do you mean?


01:10:10.567 --> 01:10:12.664
If we passed through a wormhole.
A wrinkle in the space time fabric.


01:10:12.674 --> 01:10:17.732
Theoretically, we could be in different dimension with those people who
don't exist...


01:10:17.774 --> 01:10:19.547
...or they never exist?


01:10:19.588 --> 01:10:20.577
That is insane!


01:10:20.587 --> 01:10:23.716
Stop it! That's enough!
all of you!


01:10:24.697 --> 01:10:25.824
I know what's going on here.


01:10:26.699 --> 01:10:27.669
You do?


01:10:27.700 --> 01:10:29.640
How much did they pay you?


01:10:29.869 --> 01:10:31.674
What are you talking about?


01:10:31.684 --> 01:10:34.646
I can't believe he
do this, she's her daughter!


01:10:34.687 --> 01:10:36.742
Ok. Miss, I don't know
what's going on here...


01:10:37.858 --> 01:10:39.715
Get up!


01:10:43.698 --> 01:10:44.824
Where did you get that?


01:10:44.835 --> 01:10:46.774
You!
- Yes...


01:10:46.774 --> 01:10:48.841
How much did they pay you?
- What?


01:10:48.882 --> 01:10:52.655
Where did they take her?!!!
Please! What are you talking about?


01:10:52.686 --> 01:10:54.846
My husband...
- Miss, please!


01:10:54.856 --> 01:10:56.827
Shut, just shut up!


01:10:57.630 --> 01:11:00.623
Ma'am, who's your husband?
Just tell us that.


01:11:01.697 --> 01:11:03.763
Why are you doing this?
- Listen to me...


01:11:03.877 --> 01:11:06.776
I promise you, I've never
met your husband.
.


01:11:07.714 --> 01:11:09.654
What is wrong with this?


01:11:09.716 --> 01:11:11.886
Ma'am look,
I do not know what this is...


01:11:12.794 --> 01:11:15.599
But...
- What don't I just shoot you
in the face?


01:11:15.641 --> 01:11:16.631
No!


01:11:16.736 --> 01:11:20.876
Ray, what happened to you?


01:11:20.876 --> 01:11:22.845
Why are you talking like this?


01:11:23.814 --> 01:11:26.715
You've never spoken
about God before.


01:11:26.861 --> 01:11:28.759
Where is this coming from?


01:11:28.894 --> 01:11:30.792
From...


01:11:32.669 --> 01:11:33.827
My wife.


01:11:57.645 --> 01:11:58.740
Miss, please!


01:11:58.855 --> 01:12:00.752
Forget about him, ok?


01:12:00.825 --> 01:12:02.693
He's an idiot.


01:12:02.797 --> 01:12:04.863
He's not a part of anything.
Point that gun at me.


01:12:08.814 --> 01:12:09.972
I'm an idiot?


01:12:10.743 --> 01:12:11.776
What about her?


01:12:11.942 --> 01:12:14.854
Miss, please!
Point the gun at me!


01:12:16.824 --> 01:12:17.857
Here you go.


01:12:18.691 --> 01:12:20.798
Good.


01:12:20.840 --> 01:12:24.769
Now, just tell me what you think
is going on?


01:12:24.842 --> 01:12:26.739
He is trying to take her from me.


01:12:28.712 --> 01:12:30.870
He think he can buy his way
out of anything.


01:12:30.985 --> 01:12:33.717
He took my daughter,
and that ring.


01:12:34.728 --> 01:12:35.887
I fell asleep...


01:12:37.701 --> 01:12:41.727
Somebody put something in my drink.
I should have known he will find a way.


01:12:43.876 --> 01:12:45.815
He could not have done this.


01:12:45.919 --> 01:12:46.941
There's no way.


01:12:47.880 --> 01:12:51.853
This plane landed while
I was sleeping.


01:12:51.927 --> 01:12:54.805
He took her! He paid all of you
to lie to me.


01:12:55.867 --> 01:12:57.848
I can't lose her again.
I can't...


01:12:57.868 --> 01:12:59.746
You need to listen to me.


01:13:00.820 --> 01:13:02.718
I was awake all the time.


01:13:03.719 --> 01:13:04.877
This plane never landed.


01:13:05.023 --> 01:13:07.850
No one got off this plane.


01:13:07.965 --> 01:13:09.894
Then where is she?


01:13:12.907 --> 01:13:16.746
I can't lose her, I
can't, she's all I have!


01:13:17.987 --> 01:13:21.887
You're all think I'm crazy,
what am I supposed to say?


01:13:21.960 --> 01:13:23.931
That she just disappeared?


01:13:24.797 --> 01:13:25.996
I know where she is.


01:13:56.823 --> 01:13:57.957
Pastor Barnes?


01:13:59.000 --> 01:14:00.032
Chloe...


01:14:00.835 --> 01:14:02.859
Hey....
- Oh, no...


01:14:02.973 --> 01:14:05.007
Oh, thank God
you're still here.


01:14:05.017 --> 01:14:10.055
My mom and Raymie,
when I saw that they had gone,
I was sacred that God had...


01:14:10.087 --> 01:14:14.998
He did. Chloe, just like He
promised, A blink of an eye.


01:14:16.040 --> 01:14:17.793
What?


01:14:17.835 --> 01:14:18.931
It's true...


01:14:20.839 --> 01:14:22.069
Then why are you still here?


01:14:27.930 --> 01:14:29.857
It is in the Bible.


01:14:29.930 --> 01:14:32.831
My parents sent me to
camp on summer, and...


01:14:32.872 --> 01:14:34.864
Everyone was talking about this.


01:14:35.104 --> 01:14:41.809
They say that one day
millions of people will going to
just disappear.


01:14:41.851 --> 01:14:42.883
Millions?


01:14:43.050 --> 01:14:44.928
What else did they say?


01:14:44.928 --> 01:14:46.826
I do not remember.


01:14:47.065 --> 01:14:48.933
It was a long time ago.


01:14:48.974 --> 01:14:51.842
Are you saying it was the devil?


01:14:52.040 --> 01:14:53.062
No.


01:14:53.114 --> 01:14:54.980
It was God.


01:14:56.922 --> 01:14:58.892
Don't tell me you believe this.


01:14:58.924 --> 01:15:00.986
It does not matter what I believe.


01:15:00.997 --> 01:15:03.083
Where are they?
Where did they go?


01:15:03.093 --> 01:15:04.866
To heaven.


01:15:10.884 --> 01:15:12.042
PK was right.


01:15:12.115 --> 01:15:13.992
What do you mean?


01:15:15.086 --> 01:15:17.057
Maybe I am really crazy.


01:15:17.088 --> 01:15:18.966
No, you're not.


01:15:19.998 --> 01:15:22.982
She's better off without me
- Don't say that.


01:15:24.911 --> 01:15:25.943
No, No!
Please don't!


01:15:25.953 --> 01:15:26.997
Please, do not!


01:15:27.112 --> 01:15:30.052
Maybe, the world is better off
without me.


01:15:30.125 --> 01:15:33.022
You need to listen to me now,
do not do this.


01:15:34.056 --> 01:15:35.933
You can't just give up
on her.


01:15:38.133 --> 01:15:40.906
Do you have children,
Mr. Williams?


01:15:41.104 --> 01:15:42.878
No, I don't.


01:15:44.150 --> 01:15:46.080
But I did have a mom.


01:15:46.956 --> 01:15:50.919
She was sick. My daddy tried everything...
doctors, pills...


01:15:51.023 --> 01:15:52.994
But in the end,
it didn't matter.


01:15:53.171 --> 01:15:55.069
I came home from
school one day.


01:15:56.216 --> 01:15:58.042
And I found her.


01:15:58.042 --> 01:15:59.982
She was lying there.


01:16:00.086 --> 01:16:04.047
Still. Don't you do that to Katie.


01:16:06.988 --> 01:16:11.170
We may not know what happened here today
but it is not Katie's fault...


01:16:11.170 --> 01:16:12.902
Do you hear me?


01:16:12.975 --> 01:16:14.101
Yes.


01:16:15.040 --> 01:16:17.177
But she's somewhere out there,
right now...


01:16:17.897 --> 01:16:19.023
Watching us.


01:16:26.073 --> 01:16:27.908
Yeah, that's good.


01:16:27.919 --> 01:16:28.910
Give me that.


01:16:41.224 --> 01:16:45.104
Hattie, this isn't about us.


01:16:46.043 --> 01:16:47.941
It's about the truth.


01:16:48.150 --> 01:16:50.016
You need to focus on the truth.


01:16:51.049 --> 01:16:52.186
That truth, Ray?


01:16:53.062 --> 01:16:55.085
Are you serious?
- Yes.


01:16:55.126 --> 01:16:58.098
This isn't about our past,
it's about right now.


01:16:58.192 --> 01:17:00.968
What's happening on this plane
right now.


01:17:01.176 --> 01:17:04.041
This could be happening everywhere,
right now.


01:17:04.114 --> 01:17:08.151
So they are all in heaven.
That is your conclusions.


01:17:08.161 --> 01:17:11.060
Without speaking to anyone
outside of this plane.


01:17:11.060 --> 01:17:14.032
You're gonna jump to the first explanation
that pops into your head.


01:17:14.064 --> 01:17:16.035
I already knew this
was coming.


01:17:17.036 --> 01:17:19.070
In details.


01:17:19.080 --> 01:17:20.237
How can that be possible?


01:17:21.207 --> 01:17:25.161
The way it happened,
the way they disappeared...


01:17:26.162 --> 01:17:29.217
Even the way their clothes
were still there.


01:17:29.269 --> 01:17:31.105
Perfect details.


01:17:32.200 --> 01:17:34.077
How could she know that?


01:17:34.202 --> 01:17:35.264
Think about it.


01:17:36.275 --> 01:17:38.216
Why don't you think about this?


01:17:39.249 --> 01:17:42.147
You lied to me about your wife.


01:17:43.065 --> 01:17:45.088
You lied to your wife
about this trip.


01:17:45.161 --> 01:17:47.153
You even lied to your
own daughter.


01:17:47.341 --> 01:17:51.169
It seems that you're able to lie to
just about everybody in your life.


01:17:51.169 --> 01:17:54.089
And now you're asking me
to find God.


01:17:55.184 --> 01:17:56.174
Hattie.


01:18:07.175 --> 01:18:08.270
I don't understand.


01:18:09.209 --> 01:18:11.201
You were here every day.


01:18:11.211 --> 01:18:13.244
You worked here,
you preached here.


01:18:13.286 --> 01:18:15.091
That's not what counted.


01:18:15.258 --> 01:18:16.321
What do you mean?


01:18:16.332 --> 01:18:21.108
I knew all the words, I could
quote the chapters and the verses,
but that was not enough.


01:18:21.171 --> 01:18:23.037
You have to believe.


01:18:24.142 --> 01:18:25.134
Believe?


01:18:25.311 --> 01:18:27.179
Believe in what?


01:18:28.148 --> 01:18:30.286
In a God that killed my father?


01:18:30.327 --> 01:18:38.168
A God that grabbed my mother and my brother
and raised them out of this world.
A God that crashes planes and destroys cities?


01:18:38.199 --> 01:18:40.108
He took them to protect them.


01:18:40.108 --> 01:18:41.204
From what?


01:18:41.245 --> 01:18:44.113
From the darkest time in
the history of this world.


01:18:44.321 --> 01:18:46.313
Persecution, war...


01:18:46.386 --> 01:18:50.099
In 7 years of darkness,
He took them to heaven.


01:18:51.267 --> 01:18:53.238
And what about the rest of us?


01:18:54.239 --> 01:18:57.076
What about me?
What am I supposed to do?


01:18:57.108 --> 01:19:01.278
It is not about what we do, it's about
asking for forgiveness,
it's about turning our lives over...


01:19:01.289 --> 01:19:02.311
Stop it!


01:19:03.228 --> 01:19:08.160
The God that my mother talked about,
would never do something like this.


01:19:08.337 --> 01:19:10.277
Chloe, please...


01:19:10.371 --> 01:19:12.134
Listen to me.


01:19:12.342 --> 01:19:14.136
Listen to you?


01:19:14.282 --> 01:19:16.086
Why should I?


01:19:16.252 --> 01:19:18.318
You didn't even listen to you.


01:19:38.227 --> 01:19:39.424
Are you okay Marshal?


01:19:40.269 --> 01:19:41.290
Yeah.


01:19:43.211 --> 01:19:44.368
Heard all about you.


01:19:44.368 --> 01:19:47.309
Peacon 257.
This is dispatch.


01:19:48.185 --> 01:19:50.177
This is Pancon 257,
calling dispatch.


01:19:50.188 --> 01:19:53.253
Pancon 257, This is
Marcus, are you there?


01:19:53.326 --> 01:19:58.270
Marcus, I'm 20 minutes outside of JFK.
I had to turn around.


01:19:58.302 --> 01:20:00.137
How many did you lose?


01:20:02.452 --> 01:20:04.443
So, it is everywhere.


01:20:04.454 --> 01:20:06.217
The whole planet, buddy.


01:20:08.324 --> 01:20:11.294
No one knows how many,
but millions.


01:20:11.356 --> 01:20:13.233
...


01:20:13.233 --> 01:20:14.433
What about my family?


01:20:15.371 --> 01:20:18.301
I need you to call Irene,
make sure they are safe.


01:20:18.301 --> 01:20:19.283
How's your fuel?


01:20:19.314 --> 01:20:21.411
Critical. I would be lucky to reach
the coast without ditching in.


01:20:21.421 --> 01:20:27.417
Listen, there are planes down everywhere,
the runway is full of birds,
there's no way you can get into JFK.


01:20:27.427 --> 01:20:29.201
What about LaGuardia?


01:20:29.242 --> 01:20:30.400
I'm sorry, Ray.


01:20:31.203 --> 01:20:32.267
So, where am I going?


01:20:32.277 --> 01:20:33.404
You gonna have to go inland.


01:20:34.279 --> 01:20:36.302
Marcus, I can't go inland!


01:20:36.344 --> 01:20:39.410
You need to tell me
when you're ready.


01:20:39.421 --> 01:20:43.360
Circuit is impossible, you have to talk to them.
They have to gonna clear things up for us there.


01:20:44.499 --> 01:20:46.230
Marcus?


01:20:47.241 --> 01:20:48.232
Marcus!


01:20:52.247 --> 01:20:59.390
JFK tower, this Pancon 257, I have a low-fuel emergency.
I need a runway. Repeat. I need a runway.


01:21:39.583 --> 01:21:41.376
So...


01:21:41.699 --> 01:21:43.605
Is there a backup plan?


01:21:44.575 --> 01:21:46.548
I'm gonna level with you.


01:21:47.590 --> 01:21:51.417
We're not just a low on fuel,
we're low on fumes.


01:21:51.521 --> 01:21:55.464
JFK was the closest airport,
and I would love to have
made it that far.


01:21:55.631 --> 01:21:57.539
We only have one option.


01:21:57.570 --> 01:22:00.543
I hope they clear us a runway
and hope that they do it soon.


01:22:00.584 --> 01:22:03.515
What about the water?
- Can't raise the nose.


01:22:03.515 --> 01:22:06.549
When we hit the water,
this thing is going to disintegrate.


01:22:09.500 --> 01:22:16.497
Can't. I can't let the people back there
go down without having any chance
to undo some of their mistakes.


01:22:17.676 --> 01:22:18.667
Hey...


01:22:20.481 --> 01:22:24.486
You are Venice Baxter, aren't you?
Tom's daughter.


01:22:26.499 --> 01:22:28.564
You probably do not remember me,
we...


01:22:28.595 --> 01:22:35.677
...met once at your father's office.
You were sitting right by this little
yellow desk.


01:22:36.615 --> 01:22:42.497
I remember thinking, this guy's place,
decorated with the best of everything...


01:22:42.695 --> 01:22:44.758
...but he's got this plastic little desk.


01:22:45.633 --> 01:22:50.546
Sitting beside him like it's the finest piece
of furniture in the room.


01:22:51.641 --> 01:22:54.582
Sometimes that's the only way
I got to see him.


01:22:55.791 --> 01:22:57.523
Well...


01:22:58.566 --> 01:23:00.537
At least he was trying.


01:23:00.704 --> 01:23:02.633
And I have a little girl too.


01:23:03.811 --> 01:23:07.545
I mean, she was little.
She's married now.


01:23:08.515 --> 01:23:10.486
she never had
a desk in my office.


01:23:10.527 --> 01:23:12.573
The truth is...
I was so busy.


01:23:13.824 --> 01:23:15.689
I hardly ever saw her though.


01:23:17.597 --> 01:23:23.604
You know, when all these people
disappeared, I never even thought
about her.


01:23:24.751 --> 01:23:30.550
I wish I could say I did,
but I was always thinking about money,
about opportunities...


01:23:31.666 --> 01:23:33.532
Making my next meal.


01:23:37.747 --> 01:23:38.768
I'm sorry...


01:23:39.811 --> 01:23:42.752
You know what you said
about heaven?


01:23:45.589 --> 01:23:46.817
As much as I want
to see her...


01:23:48.767 --> 01:23:51.824
When I get home,
I hope she's not there.


01:24:15.623 --> 01:24:18.853
I need you try and
call Chloe for me.


01:24:19.729 --> 01:24:21.763
I've been trying.


01:24:22.629 --> 01:24:27.635
The truth is...uh... I've not stopped
thinking about her since I
got on the plane.


01:24:28.750 --> 01:24:30.837
I can understand that.


01:24:33.861 --> 01:24:38.595
JFK tower, do you hear me?


01:24:38.700 --> 01:24:41.641
We are headed for the coast.


01:24:41.641 --> 01:24:43.674
Our fuel is at critical.


01:24:43.716 --> 01:24:44.874
I need a clear runway.


01:24:44.916 --> 01:24:48.814
I repeat, I need
a clear runway.


01:24:49.617 --> 01:24:50.743
Listen to me...


01:24:50.826 --> 01:24:52.695
I have a plane full of people here.


01:24:52.695 --> 01:24:54.749
I have no spoilers, no flaps,
no elevators and...


01:24:54.801 --> 01:24:56.865
And if I run this thing right,
no reverse thrust...


01:24:56.938 --> 01:24:59.879
I need some room!


01:25:28.765 --> 01:25:30.706
Oh...


01:25:31.739 --> 01:25:33.647
...


01:25:34.815 --> 01:25:36.785
Were you with her...


01:25:36.817 --> 01:25:39.654
When she got the concert tickets?


01:25:39.862 --> 01:25:42.887
I was... what can I say...


01:25:42.939 --> 01:25:44.868
She was hurt.


01:25:46.809 --> 01:25:49.739
I should never have
left her today.


01:25:49.843 --> 01:25:50.831
You didn't know.


01:25:50.884 --> 01:25:53.950
All I knew she came home
and see me and I left.


01:25:53.981 --> 01:25:56.860
I left her alone.


01:25:56.933 --> 01:26:00.802
God only knows what she's
been going through down there.


01:26:00.833 --> 01:26:04.900
She loves you, Ray?
She will understand.


01:26:10.898 --> 01:26:14.850
I can't let that be the last thing
we said to each other.


01:26:16.997 --> 01:26:20.805
I just...
I can't.


01:26:21.773 --> 01:26:23.838
I need to tell her the truth.


01:26:23.890 --> 01:26:28.791
And I need her to know that
this wasn't her mother's fault.
It's all mine.


01:26:29.865 --> 01:26:35.904
Every time that Irene mentioned God,
I walked away.


01:27:38.006 --> 01:27:39.872
Mom...


01:27:41.040 --> 01:27:44.847
I don't know if you can hear me...


01:27:45.055 --> 01:27:48.820
But I just wanted to say...


01:27:49.884 --> 01:27:54.066
This morning, I felt like
our family was falling apart.


01:27:54.108 --> 01:27:56.858
And I blamed you.


01:27:56.942 --> 01:28:01.010
And I know that I hurt you.


01:28:01.876 --> 01:28:04.013
And I'm sorry.


01:28:04.993 --> 01:28:07.851
I'm so sorry.


01:28:26.069 --> 01:28:27.862
Hello?


01:28:27.904 --> 01:28:30.074
Who is this?
- Chloe...


01:28:30.105 --> 01:28:32.086
This is Buck.
- Buck?


01:28:33.880 --> 01:28:36.081
Thank God, you're alive.


01:28:36.154 --> 01:28:37.917
Where is my dad?


01:28:37.959 --> 01:28:39.950
He is here.


01:28:40.899 --> 01:28:42.922
Chloe, are you okay?


01:28:42.932 --> 01:28:44.131
Dad...


01:28:44.872 --> 01:28:46.072
I thought you were dead.


01:28:46.103 --> 01:28:48.137
Are you okay?


01:28:50.056 --> 01:28:53.884
Yeah... I guess so.


01:28:54.061 --> 01:28:59.930
But Mom and Raymie,
they are both gone.


01:29:05.113 --> 01:29:07.136
Mom told me about this.


01:29:07.188 --> 01:29:10.025
I know, she told me too.


01:29:10.057 --> 01:29:12.925
I love you so much,
sweetheart.


01:29:13.029 --> 01:29:16.001
I love you more than anything
in the world.


01:29:16.064 --> 01:29:19.099
Me too daddy, me too...


01:29:19.109 --> 01:29:22.175
I'm so sorry I lied to you and
I wasn't there with you today.


01:29:22.216 --> 01:29:25.920
I really, really need you to know
how much I love you.


01:29:25.962 --> 01:29:27.119
No matter what happens.


01:29:27.161 --> 01:29:31.058
Wait, dad... Why
are you talking like this?


01:29:31.100 --> 01:29:33.061
What's going on?
Where are you?


01:29:33.061 --> 01:29:38.036
Well... we still are in the air. We're
on our way home, but there is a problem.


01:29:38.078 --> 01:29:42.041
The airports are closed,
the roads are jammed
and there's no way to land...


01:29:42.051 --> 01:29:43.031
What?


01:29:43.052 --> 01:29:46.034
And I do not have enough fuel.


01:29:46.055 --> 01:29:48.027
Chloe...


01:29:48.235 --> 01:29:50.134
Dad...


01:29:51.073 --> 01:29:52.981
Chloe...


01:30:48.198 --> 01:30:50.191
Ladies and gentlemen...


01:30:50.993 --> 01:30:52.256
We are coming in on New York.


01:30:52.298 --> 01:30:54.175
Alright...


01:30:56.177 --> 01:30:59.118
However, we still have
challenges ahead.
All the airports are closed.


01:30:59.181 --> 01:31:02.213
I need you to remain in your seats...


01:31:02.244 --> 01:31:07.199
With your seat belts fastened,
and try to remain calm.


01:31:07.230 --> 01:31:10.170
But I have to be honest...


01:31:11.109 --> 01:31:14.009
This is a very serious situation.


01:31:14.040 --> 01:31:19.108
We're talking to the ground, we'll try
to find an alternate landing sites.


01:31:19.160 --> 01:31:22.217
But we are very low on fuel.


01:31:24.104 --> 01:31:28.098
Please pay very close attention
to our flight crew.


01:31:28.234 --> 01:31:31.113
And if you believe in prayer...


01:31:33.081 --> 01:31:35.177
Now would be the time.


01:31:39.161 --> 01:31:40.152
Will you pray with me?


01:31:40.204 --> 01:31:43.177
Yes, of course.
Yeah.


01:31:59.102 --> 01:32:00.072
Nothing.


01:32:00.103 --> 01:32:01.167
Still can't get signal.


01:32:01.240 --> 01:32:02.303
Keep trying.


01:32:02.314 --> 01:32:04.210
I will.


01:32:04.387 --> 01:32:07.215
Well, we'll gonna have to
put it down.


01:32:07.319 --> 01:32:09.289
Put it down?


01:32:09.321 --> 01:32:11.260
Where?
- Water...


01:32:11.291 --> 01:32:12.219
But you said...


01:32:12.230 --> 01:32:14.096
I know...


01:32:14.169 --> 01:32:19.134
I wait on JFK as long as I can, but
I can't fly there without a clear runway.


01:32:19.145 --> 01:32:21.345
There's nothing but sitting on
every side of the airport.


01:32:22.117 --> 01:32:25.173
By flying in,
there's nowhere to land.


01:32:25.225 --> 01:32:29.250
We're flying a 400-tonne
missile right into Queens.


01:32:58.262 --> 01:33:02.330
JFK tower, this is Pancon 257, we need
emergency clearance immediately.


01:33:02.371 --> 01:33:05.195
Get her back!
Keep trying.


01:33:19.233 --> 01:33:24.228
Ok folks, I need your full attention
as we go through the emergency procedures.


01:33:24.280 --> 01:33:37.229
Underneath your seats, you will find your life jackets.
You must keep your seat belts tightly fastened
across your waists until the plane come to a complete stop.


01:33:37.231 --> 01:33:40.235
Then you must follow all
flight crew's instructions.


01:33:40.246 --> 01:33:44.375
JFK tower, This is Pancon 257, we need
emergency clearance right now.


01:33:44.416 --> 01:33:50.414
JFK tower. JFK tower, This is Pancon 257,
we need clearance now!


01:34:04.264 --> 01:34:06.193
Come on...


01:34:20.291 --> 01:34:22.230
OK.


01:34:27.279 --> 01:34:28.363
Buck, can you hear me?


01:34:28.405 --> 01:34:29.333
Chloe


01:34:29.375 --> 01:34:31.408
Turn on the speakers.


01:34:33.327 --> 01:34:35.383
I think I found a place for
you guys to land.


01:34:35.456 --> 01:34:40.365
The new East-West highway
near the mall. No one's out here. I think
I can clear enough room.


01:34:40.365 --> 01:34:43.337
Our guidance system is out. I won't be able
to find it in the dark.


01:34:43.369 --> 01:34:47.405
Hey, Chloe, your phone...
you should open up the compass app.


01:34:47.447 --> 01:34:50.284
Ok, hang on.


01:34:52.265 --> 01:34:53.287
Ok, I've got it.


01:34:53.318 --> 01:34:57.531
Well, you see the bottom,
those little numbers?
I need you to read those to me.


01:34:58.334 --> 01:35:06.302
40.66.34 North 73.78.32 West


01:35:06.355 --> 01:35:07.376
I got it.


01:35:07.418 --> 01:35:09.355
Chloe, how much room we've got?


01:35:09.355 --> 01:35:10.523
Uh... about half a mile away.


01:35:10.555 --> 01:35:11.493
And there's more...


01:35:11.535 --> 01:35:14.435
How much more?
I need at least a mile.


01:35:14.435 --> 01:35:16.427
Okay, hang on.


01:35:43.394 --> 01:35:46.335
Chloe... Chloe, are you still there?


01:35:50.371 --> 01:35:52.374
Abbout seven-tenth.


01:35:52.416 --> 01:35:54.408
Eight-tenth...


01:35:54.449 --> 01:35:57.484
Buck... Buck, can you hear me?


01:35:58.391 --> 01:36:00.362
Hello?


01:36:11.384 --> 01:36:12.614
Come on.


01:36:17.527 --> 01:36:19.560
You've got to be kidding me.


01:36:20.572 --> 01:36:22.542
Come on!


01:36:27.518 --> 01:36:32.399
We need a visual of some kind,
so we can see where the landing zone begins.


01:36:44.442 --> 01:36:48.561
How are you?
you mind if I sit down here for a moment?
- Yes... Yes...


01:36:48.593 --> 01:36:53.442
Just until your husband
comes back from the bathroom.


01:37:06.635 --> 01:37:07.626
We ran out of fuel!


01:37:07.667 --> 01:37:09.566
What?


01:37:09.577 --> 01:37:10.630
No.


01:37:10.682 --> 01:37:13.651
We can still land it.
We can glide it down.


01:37:13.683 --> 01:37:19.420
But we're going to hit the ground fast.
I've no thrust to slow it down,
just the brakes.


01:37:19.451 --> 01:37:22.402
We're going to need
every inch of the gas.


01:37:29.546 --> 01:37:30.474
Dad...


01:37:30.516 --> 01:37:31.506
Chloe...


01:37:31.517 --> 01:37:32.507
Go ahead...


01:37:32.549 --> 01:37:37.430
I'm out of road. I'm at nine-tenth of a mile
but there're a bunch of heavy equipment
blocking my way.


01:37:37.492 --> 01:37:39.463
Honey, nine-tenth
is good enough?


01:37:39.494 --> 01:37:44.437
But I need a bright visual point
of referrence so that I can see where
the landing zone is.


01:37:44.468 --> 01:37:47.440
Okay.
I'm flashing my lights.
Can you see that?


01:37:47.481 --> 01:37:51.476
No, we are too far out for that, I need
a bigger light like a flare.


01:37:51.486 --> 01:37:54.626
But we are running out of time.
I have to come in right now!


01:37:54.667 --> 01:37:56.608
Chloe...


01:38:03.678 --> 01:38:06.661
Where are your
smoke up matches?


01:38:11.698 --> 01:38:13.565
There isn't enough room, is there?


01:38:13.607 --> 01:38:17.431
If there isn't, I don't want her
to think it's her fault.


01:38:40.594 --> 01:38:42.754
This is it, we're coming down.


01:38:42.795 --> 01:38:44.736
Can you see anything?


01:38:44.767 --> 01:38:49.572
No.
- Keep looking.
We have about three miles.


01:38:58.563 --> 01:39:01.691
We've got one try.
We need to know where to start.


01:39:01.733 --> 01:39:03.610
Nothing yet!


01:39:03.610 --> 01:39:05.664
Come on, honey.


01:39:11.692 --> 01:39:13.622
There!


01:39:58.828 --> 01:40:01.790
Try to lock the landing gear!


01:40:23.637 --> 01:40:25.827
Dad, you've got no back wheels!


01:41:18.752 --> 01:41:19.879
Oh...


01:41:19.889 --> 01:41:22.723
We're home!


01:41:24.966 --> 01:41:29.742
Everyone ok? I need everyone
out of the plane now.
Everyone get up!


01:42:00.871 --> 01:42:03.770
One at a time.
Let's go!


01:42:05.002 --> 01:42:05.982
Let's go...


01:42:06.013 --> 01:42:09.975
When you get to the bottom,
please get out of the way
for others.


01:42:22.887 --> 01:42:24.876
Hey, hey


01:42:26.817 --> 01:42:27.986
Hey!


01:42:50.772 --> 01:42:53.005
Buck!
- Chloe.


01:42:53.881 --> 01:42:55.943
Thank you.


01:43:01.794 --> 01:43:03.953
You did a great job.


01:43:05.798 --> 01:43:06.999
You too.


01:43:06.999 --> 01:43:08.948
Hattie!


01:43:11.951 --> 01:43:13.944
I'm sorry.


01:43:14.851 --> 01:43:16.050
I know.


01:43:23.069 --> 01:43:25.009
Dad...


01:43:27.937 --> 01:43:29.941
I should be here with you.


01:43:30.014 --> 01:43:33.861
With mom, with Raymie.
I shouldn't have left.


01:43:34.831 --> 01:43:36.989
I'm just glad you're okay.


01:43:40.911 --> 01:43:42.997
I thought you might want this.


01:44:04.989 --> 01:44:07.827
Looks like the end of the world.


01:44:07.962 --> 01:44:10.903
No. Not yet.


01:44:12.040 --> 01:44:14.960
I'm afraid this is
just the beginning.

